               <exData contentType="text/html">
                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="font-weight:bold;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">Grad PLUS Information &amp; Application Process<span style="font-weight:normal"><br/>The Federal Direct Graduate PLUS is a low-interest credit based loan available to graduate students pursuing Master’s and Doctoral degrees and is not subsidized by the federal government. In order to apply:<br/></span><br/>• Must have a FAFSA on file to be considered for eligibility for current year.<span style="font-weight:normal"><br/>• Log on to<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span><a href="www.studentaid.gov" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt">www.studentaid.gov</a><span style="font-weight:normal"> and complete the following (you will need your FSA ID available at<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">  </span></span><a href="www.studentaid.gov/fsa-id">www.studentaid.gov/fsa-id</a><span style="font-weight:normal"> ):<br/><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">          </span>o Master promissory note (MPN)<br/><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">          </span>o Grad Plus loan entrance counseling (if you have not already done so)<br/><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">          </span>o Grad PLUS application and credit check</span><br/>*<span style="text-decoration:underline">NOTE</span>:<span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:italic"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span><span style="font-weight:normal">Additionally,<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span><span style="text-decoration:underline">PLUS credit counseling</span><span style="font-weight:normal"> will be required by the U.S. Department of Education if you have an adverse credit history and still wish to pursue a loan with an endorser or by satisfactorily documenting extenuating circumstances.</span></p><p style="text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p></body>
               </exData>
